<code>assert (\result >= 0) => this.get(\result).equals(o);</code>
--------------------
<code>assert (\result >= 0) => (this.get(\result) != null && this.get(\result).equals(o));</code>
--------------------
<code>assert (\result >= 0) => Objects.equals(this.get(\result), o);</code>

This assert statement ensures that if the `indexOf` method returns a non-negative index, the element at that index in the vector is equal to the specified element `o`. Note that `Objects.equals` is used to compare the elements, as per the method's documentation.
